# configMapGenerator input for `hope-lmstudio-config` (EXECUTION-PLAN §14.4 item 2).
#
# DELIBERATELY EMPTY, and that is the correct end state rather than a stub to
# fill in later.
#
# Everything this workload needs at runtime is either:
#
#   * baked into the IMAGE, because it is a property of the artifact and must
#     not be weakenable from a manifest — HOPE_EXPECT_ACCEL is the load-bearing
#     example (00-project-context.md §Configuration Principles: an engine
#     selection is not a manifest knob), or
#   * set explicitly on the Deployment's container, where it sits next to the
#     comment explaining why (LMS_SERVER_HOST, HOPE_ACCEL_ENFORCE, LMS_LOAD), or
#   * DB-tier config resolved tenant -> SYSTEM through `AiProviderConnection` /
#     `AiTaskDefault`, which is where the base URL, the model selection and any
#     credential belong.
#
# Adding a key here would move a value OUT of the governed tier and into an
# env var that cannot change without a restart (09-infrastructure-devops.md
# §Configuration Tiers L1). If you find yourself wanting one, check first that
# it is not really a `db-config` / `global-kv` value.
#
# The file exists so the configMapGenerator entry and the `envFrom` shape match
# every other workload in the repo.
